{#-
  DERIVED, not from upstream. OpenClaw's agent-core compaction is a conversation
  summarizer and ships no observation-level prompt. This template keeps OpenClaw's
  own preservation discipline -- exact paths, names, error messages; no invention;
  no continuing the conversation -- and moves it onto the single-observation task
  that ACON equation (4) defines.

  Why not reuse the history template: it emits a structured checkpoint with Goal /
  Progress / Next Steps sections, which is a summary of a conversation. Handing
  that back in place of an observation would replace a tool reply with a project
  status, which is a different method.
-#}
<observation>
{{ observation }}
</observation>

<current-task>
{{ task }}
</current-task>

<work-so-far>
{{ history }}
</work-so-far>

The observation above is the reply from the most recent tool call, and it is too long to keep in full. Produce a refined version of that observation, and nothing else.

RULES:
- Keep every value the agent will need for its next actions: exact ids, paths, field names, counts, statuses, timestamps and error messages, verbatim.
- Drop what cannot be acted on: boilerplate, repeated schema descriptions, prompt echoes, padding, and entries already covered by <work-so-far>.
- If the observation is a list, keep the entries that matter and say how many were omitted. Do not silently summarise a list into a count.
- If the observation contains an error or a refusal, keep it in full. A dropped error causes the same call to be retried forever.
- Do NOT invent values. Anything not present in the observation must not appear in the refinement.
- Do NOT continue the task, answer questions, or propose next steps. Only rewrite the observation.

Use this EXACT format:

# Reasoning
[What the next steps need from this observation, and what can be dropped]

# Refined Observation
[The refined observation]
